#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096350 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "12811582-7156-5b84-9ba9-5545f87894f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-3993" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "c7373a16-c90a-5875-8b17-8724542b35ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-493" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "672d52f6-89d8-550d-863b-7c5157d59ca3" :question/math-academy-id "e-494" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c8a9b38-30a3-52b1-9fff-2a4d191e1c43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300057} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0aee70-f173-5908-827f-5f89cb4c0afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300058} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8e01d5-889e-5b4a-9acb-3c0c035897a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300059} {:answer/id #uuid "736ab1b5-d37e-536f-886c-19bb16961a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300060} {:answer/id #uuid "d3877c7f-5c76-5950-9f56-cf76e73251f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3877c7f-5c76-5950-9f56-cf76e73251f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300061} :answer-field/id #uuid "12cfabff-92bf-56e2-9172-fe6f118c2de8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e6583e6-92e6-5c07-b4f7-1730072676de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114553" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72777a21-401f-5678-9b00-c73119d4e69a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300064} {:answer/id #uuid "133ed4fd-7ae8-5543-8c8f-0d689e1c9f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300065} {:answer/id #uuid "f602bd11-ba18-5d65-80f8-e2972b3cabbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300066} {:answer/id #uuid "dda2229a-76c1-5f0d-ab3a-4ac41fa9ac53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300067} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc6ee36-3b03-5351-8102-7e2618eb170b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "133ed4fd-7ae8-5543-8c8f-0d689e1c9f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300065} :answer-field/id #uuid "a75af52e-b616-5efd-9d80-047070c42974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fe9b973-85cd-5569-aae4-2db535d24d76" :question/math-academy-id "q-114555" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=8{x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 8{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\cdot (2{x}^{4})-\\int \\frac{2{x}^{4}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e32fa8-90ab-5f78-a1da-cf421141cb00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300071} {:answer/id #uuid "8193345e-f5e5-5582-9492-3d0696344172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300072} {:answer/id #uuid "4ba52cda-c7be-5591-a551-1a8aca9e19bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300073} {:answer/id #uuid "839ff85f-c34c-5c3c-b037-815079fd6655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300074} {:answer/id #uuid "40e0240f-2655-5b8d-956c-6b0ceb344a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19e32fa8-90ab-5f78-a1da-cf421141cb00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300071} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeb504cb-d712-53f5-9c85-be74cc3f59eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a4eb688e-c5f1-5e1b-a808-764b83388ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114556" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285bdb56-5409-582c-800d-189504dbf9ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1}{4{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300078} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5551ec-5a91-5363-81d0-33b0cb469957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300079} {:answer/id #uuid "e31068fc-b371-575f-a19f-d589ea2f95f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300080} {:answer/id #uuid "8a87d984-3417-54ea-becb-78dd91989f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300081} {:answer/id #uuid "b165f745-5390-5660-a992-74e8fb8ae3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a87d984-3417-54ea-becb-78dd91989f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300081} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f211b5-dbbd-5025-9531-2d53fbdf405e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5bbf57b0-6d8b-508e-9a69-4026c9515f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-114557" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})-\\int (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0aef57-abe2-5e9b-8ffd-b4ac250e8856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300085} {:answer/id #uuid "9fec5b92-742f-5131-b6ee-8697e0573919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300086} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4d5c0b-b085-55f3-bba7-69a470201edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-\\frac{x}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300087} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf8ad37-97c5-52c4-9f50-a7d3b497740a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300088} {:answer/id #uuid "260a2b08-273c-5530-b4b4-c3d9f234169d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "260a2b08-273c-5530-b4b4-c3d9f234169d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300089} :answer-field/id #uuid "507e7950-22fa-5522-8d6e-e608954b5950" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df4a8ff9-b6f1-509e-8da7-ab67f79ced45" :question/math-academy-id "q-114579" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da8e5247-bf52-58e7-975b-3f66820670b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300092} {:answer/id #uuid "7c70f475-b1d5-5e18-95d2-9e7c922f108d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300093} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9bb09f-ba9a-558b-a38f-4a830e721b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300094} {:answer/id #uuid "01007e7f-0a9b-5ac6-b36d-8e9f915bf27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300095} {:answer/id #uuid "79dfeb14-bf2b-5497-bb34-51386778e9d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01007e7f-0a9b-5ac6-b36d-8e9f915bf27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300095} :answer-field/id #uuid "db580e37-a8f2-560e-b595-86510254902c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1883a81f-d78c-537f-b99d-5e0b9aacac58" :question/math-academy-id "q-114585" :question/problem "$\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{2x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $2x+1=u,$ thus $2x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int (\\frac{2x}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{u}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡u}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{2x+1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7705c3a4-0e35-509d-9808-fa04f351083f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300099} {:answer/id #uuid "2523163f-f6c8-593f-84d3-2cc72115ce70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300100} {:answer/id #uuid "b7142bcd-73dd-5cf7-b9e8-132f3589d839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300101} {:answer/id #uuid "1a2bdbe1-f3b7-5f26-82ea-a5b7f432f8ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300102} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0193d2-3eaf-54be-ab46-a92ca0576550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a0193d2-3eaf-54be-ab46-a92ca0576550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300103} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ea2e213-fe2f-5dc2-9ef9-784bd287e6a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61e03c45-6b55-5bc8-8f4d-4ef143900018" :question/math-academy-id "q-114597" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x){|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-x{|}_{1/3}^{e}\\, \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-(e-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+e-e+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98b283cb-6c59-5a0f-8573-54fa471f7356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\ln x + 2}{x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094269} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8dfc3b-eb1f-52e4-ace6-343a7c46618a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094270} {:answer/id #uuid "e81bf1f8-844b-5dd4-a69e-d1ce8972fa3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x + 2}{4x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094271} {:answer/id #uuid "fd86a01e-9451-55d1-a019-988a3ace1a4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x + 1}{2x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094272} {:answer/id #uuid "67de0f22-0b54-5707-bb69-7cd76166d425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67de0f22-0b54-5707-bb69-7cd76166d425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094273} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f9df16-6da1-5faf-9b43-d505c6ce5157" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ce071f41-118b-504d-a520-d6c46fbbaaf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-12570" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058af3d2-4de9-51f1-b45e-c4f6450388df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300106} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb1ad74-0ddf-591a-a83b-388cef01dd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300107} {:answer/id #uuid "d79fb862-748b-5e76-ab02-bc440f18ad12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300108} {:answer/id #uuid "caaad1f2-f17b-50eb-b0e1-dddf4b14cf61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{x}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300109} {:answer/id #uuid "af3459a1-862b-5808-a104-ece7d60650b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cb1ad74-0ddf-591a-a83b-388cef01dd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300107} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e0d112d-a83b-571f-8593-0c01ad5a42de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "252da65e-a015-52db-8aca-5c1050a5b779" :question/math-academy-id "q-12573" :question/problem "$\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int (x+7)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x-7\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031bf082-77a5-50b2-bbc9-0b0aae1d4c2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^3}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300113} {:answer/id #uuid "e33c738d-a3f4-5682-833f-dbc29b7a6f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^3}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e33c738d-a3f4-5682-833f-dbc29b7a6f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^3}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300114} :answer-field/id #uuid "b87aac84-1410-5551-b4fb-311889aa660e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e48be342-f105-55aa-a661-6f4ddf44b83d" :question/math-academy-id "q-346521" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,(x){|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3}}{4})\\,(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4})\\,(\\frac{1}{4})]-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2{e}^{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e9e0ecc-16be-54a5-9fce-490c475ff59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112}{9}e^9-\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300117} {:answer/id #uuid "7e40235f-ddd1-5b91-96eb-82793327b786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112}{9}e^9+\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e40235f-ddd1-5b91-96eb-82793327b786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{112}{9}e^9+\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300118} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e56c318-0074-58c5-b739-f9192314f52e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9b8ff269-1424-55b4-84ed-67c003d12084" :question/math-academy-id "q-350964" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}7{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=7{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 7{x}^{2}\\,dx=\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}7{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})(\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{7({e}^{3})^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({e}^{3})^{2})}{3}-\\frac{7(1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1)^{2})}{3}]-\\frac{14}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7{e}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{6})}{3}-\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =14{e}^{9}-(\\frac{14{e}^{9}}{9}-\\frac{14}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(126{e}^{9}-14{e}^{9}+14) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}(8{e}^{9}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3706d4b6-6af3-5407-a509-caf27e00c6bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{e}^{-4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300121} {:answer/id #uuid "79edb51e-31bf-58da-8d9a-3876cb60f095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-5{e}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300122} {:answer/id #uuid "dc063778-1fcc-5e34-aff7-aeab4d4a27a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-5{e}^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300123} {:answer/id #uuid "8d69b0c8-17df-5bd0-959c-85219414766c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{5}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300124} {:answer/id #uuid "4347eaca-a588-5bb2-a088-8cfd61908654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-4{e}^{-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc063778-1fcc-5e34-aff7-aeab4d4a27a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-5{e}^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300123} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd054f15-2a74-59d9-8154-9f8487b6d2cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64016032-3db7-586b-bd02-0efaddca45c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-49716" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,dx=-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(-\\frac{1}{x}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}(-\\frac{1}{x})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4})(-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)(-\\frac{1}{1})]+{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{x}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{e}^{4}}-(\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  & =1-5{e}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c805eea-d7ab-5933-aa2e-676591efd3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300128} {:answer/id #uuid "f6fc9108-7748-5b9a-9b90-e43d8e6b1222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{e}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300129} {:answer/id #uuid "5171b084-ff23-530e-a0d3-2d4d1456ae5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{3}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300130} {:answer/id #uuid "ae38d866-6ea9-5cec-8554-f80a8737e1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300131} {:answer/id #uuid "26fe678a-5530-5eea-8fe7-3d770cc0657a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{e}^{3}-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6fc9108-7748-5b9a-9b90-e43d8e6b1222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{e}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300129} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb1911c3-8a81-51b6-820e-711e4c21c602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5038b062-144f-58db-8c18-619c12a2718f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78883" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}9\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 9\\sqrt{x}\\,dx=6{x}^{3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}9\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(6{x}^{3/2}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{6{x}^{3/2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})(6{({e}^{2})}^{3/2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1(6(1)^{3/2})]-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}6\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-4{x}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-(4{({e}^{2})}^{3/2}-4(1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3}+4 \\\\  & =8{e}^{3}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a39ef54d-fdf7-5321-ae0c-4dd7560b65c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300135} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd9bed0-a5e8-502b-a71b-f8e4960f863b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300136} {:answer/id #uuid "5291b6f8-e057-570d-bc40-27e97e5d6a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300137} {:answer/id #uuid "0a22ac3b-850b-5111-8490-aa88cd470302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a39ef54d-fdf7-5321-ae0c-4dd7560b65c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300135} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca2a420-07b7-59b4-a0f5-01f083a15766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2ce12b4-39fc-58da-90fb-99d831518db3" :question/math-academy-id "q-78957" :question/problem "$\\int 9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 3{x}^{3}-\\int 3{x}^{3}(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3521934-f36f-5ef0-b806-afdb329e3c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300141} {:answer/id #uuid "b7428390-750b-5084-873b-8a8b645f41a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300142} {:answer/id #uuid "891afc57-76e7-51ca-aede-21264ec11dbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300143} {:answer/id #uuid "93161ec1-c844-5d3c-a140-ce0ff6d366fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300144} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa3d80c-ab19-528d-906f-c1b2436c1e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891afc57-76e7-51ca-aede-21264ec11dbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300143} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e81f80-e4a9-5d16-b74c-78c47753826b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbf7c630-44ce-52c1-83dd-093ebe2d7594" :question/math-academy-id "q-78969" :question/problem "$\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 2\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}]}
